Report placed mapping as unsupported on noncoherent ION.

The CPU-only boundary probe reproduces BUS_ADRALN on x1s CPU 7 for all
three uncached ION sizes when libc memset crosses the memfd/ION boundary.
Separate-region fills, cached ION, and CPU 0 pass. Preserving uncached
HOST_COHERENT allocations is required for GPU correctness. The backend
therefore records this allocator limitation and PanVK consistently omits
the optional extension and its features. Other allocator backends keep
existing behavior. This does not claim a placed-map CTS pass or full
conformance; the original unmodified CTS crash remains preserved.

--- a/src/panfrost/lib/kmod/pan_kmod.h
+++ b/src/panfrost/lib/kmod/pan_kmod.h
@@ -282,6 +282,8 @@
     */
    bool is_io_coherent;
 
+   bool has_unsafe_placed_mmap;
+
    /* Bitmask encoding the available GPU page sizes */
    uint64_t pgsize_bitmap;
 };
